{"id": "unknown-2026-10-12-005", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth", "improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vietnam-Cambodia trade grows as countries pursue $20 bn target", "content": "Vietnam-Cambodia bilateral trade rose 8.3 per cent year on year to $8.7 billion in the first eight months of 2026, as both countries pursue a $20 billion target. \nGrowth is supported by complementary industries, Vietnamese investment in Cambodia and improved border infrastructure, with better transport links expected to reduce logistics costs and strengthen cross-border supply chains. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-cambodia-trade-grows-as-countries-pursue-20-bn-target-314178-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-12-006", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh releases $40.6 bn export incentives for FY27", "content": "Bangladesh has released Tk 5 billion (~$40.6 million) to Bangladesh Bank for incentives and financial aid to export-oriented sectors in FY 2026-27. \nThe CGA issued debit authority on September 30 under the Finance Division's subsidies and incentives budget. \nThe allocation covers textiles, leather goods, seafood and other approved exports, plus 1 per cent aid for RMG exports. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-releases-40-6-bn-export-incentives-for-fy27-314175-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-12-007", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh seeks end to Indian anti-dumping duties on jute, PET film", "content": "Bangladesh has urged India to remove land port export restrictions and anti-dumping duties on Bangladeshi jute products and PET film at the 16th Joint Working Group on Trade meeting in New Delhi.\nDhaka also sought continued tariff preferences after LDC graduation, improved border infrastructure, faster cargo clearance and stronger regional connectivity to boost bilateral trade.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-seeks-end-to-indian-anti-dumping-duties-on-jute-pet-film-314170-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-12-008", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India, ASEAN seek faster progress on trade agreement review", "content": "ASEAN hosted the 15th AITIGA Joint Committee in Jakarta from October 6-9, where India and ASEAN reviewed negotiations on the trade-in-goods pact and directed sub-committees to accelerate pending review chapters.\nThree of eight sub-committees met on legal issues, market access and rules of origin.\nThe next hybrid Joint Committee meeting is due in India in January 2027.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-asean-seek-faster-progress-on-trade-agreement-review-314172-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-12-009", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s ₹10,000-cr SME fund: Can textile exporters tap it?", "content": "India’s ₹10,000-crore (~$1.03 billion) SME Growth Fund could help textile exporters fund capacity, technology and compliance, but it is not confirmed financing.\nThe AIF has ₹500 crore budgeted for FY2026–27 and is designed for direct equity in mainly manufacturing-focused SMEs.\nWith no textile allocation, manager or eligibility rules yet, exporters should focus on audited, investment-ready plans.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-10-000-cr-sme-fund-can-textile-exporters-tap-it--314174-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-12-010", "date": "2026-10-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Germany’s €9.3 bn footwear market and the rise of sneakers", "content": "Germany’s footwear market is forecast to shrink for a third year in 2026, but TexPro says textile-upper imports rose 0.5 per cent to $3.06 billion in January-July.\nHS 640419 footwear with textile uppers and rubber or plastic soles grew 6.3 per cent to $1.94 billion, while specified textile sports shoes fell 8.5 per cent.\nChina and Vietnam lead supply; EU inventory rules sharpen sourcing.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/germany-s-9-3-bn-footwear-market-and-the-rise-of-sneakers-314168-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
